<h1>About Math Worksheet Studio</h1>
<p>Math Worksheet Studio is an independent, browser-based collection of free printable math worksheet generators for teachers, parents and adult supervisors. Choose a topic, number range and difficulty, then print a student question sheet or matching answer key. It is not an official school curriculum or exam board.</p>
<h2>How a worksheet stays reproducible</h2>
<p>Each supported topic has a specific question generator, not a keyword-only template. The math topic, selected options, generator version and seed determine a practice set. Using the same settings reproduces the same questions and answers. Worksheets and PDF files are created in the browser, without requiring student registration or a student-grade database.</p>
<h2>How accuracy is checked</h2>
<p>Automated tests in our <a href="https://github.com/garrison2025/Math_Works">public development repository</a> compare generated problems and answers against independent calculations and check printable PDFs, layouts and browser behavior. These are software checks, not a claim that every possible problem has been manually reviewed by a teacher. Before distributing any worksheet, read its separate answer key and verify that the chosen method and difficulty match your class.</p>
<p>Some mathematical conventions vary: for example, box plots use an <strong>exclusive median-of-halves</strong> quartile method. Topics marked with worked steps expose only steps that have actually been implemented and checked. The printable protractor must be printed at 100% size and its 50 mm check line measured with a physical ruler before use.</p>
<h2>Questions, corrections and accessibility reports</h2>
<p>Found a calculation error, unclear diagram, inaccessible control or PDF printing issue? Send the topic URL, generator seed, difficulty, selected options, expected result and observed result to <a href="mailto:contact@mathworksheetstudio.com">contact@mathworksheetstudio.com</a>. We can reproduce a reported sheet without needing a child's personal information.</p>
<p>You can also use the public <a href="https://github.com/garrison2025/Math_Works/issues">issue tracker</a> for non-private technical reports. Do not post student names, classroom records or completed student worksheets in a public issue or email.</p>
<h2>What this site does not claim</h2>
<p>Our Easy, Standard and Challenge settings are generator controls, not certified grade levels. A selected worksheet may not match every school's notation, assessed scope or curriculum. Teacher judgement and physical print calibration remain essential. We do not promise any particular learning outcome, official accreditation or complete coverage of every keyword listed in outside research sources.</p>
<p><a href="/worksheets/">Browse the working worksheet library</a> or <a href="/contact/">contact the project</a>.</p>
